# Push to GitHub main

The owner has given standing permission: after every completed change, commit and push to `origin/main`. Do not open a pull request.

- Work on `main`. Commit with a concise message that explains why.
- `git push origin main` (no force push, no `--no-verify`).
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials) or unrelated local artifacts (e.g. `.audit/` screenshots) unless asked.
- If there is nothing to commit, do not create an empty commit. Still push if `main` is ahead of origin.
